    "summary": "`MissionNotFoundError` and `CrewMemberNotFoundError` are each defined as separate `Exception` subclasses in multiple service modules instead of one shared domain-error type.",
    "failure_scenario": "`MissionNotFoundError` exists independently in services/mission.py:51, services/matcher.py:73, and services/assignment.py:49; `CrewMemberNotFoundError` exists independently in services/crew.py:38 and services/assignment.py:57 — same name, same semantic meaning (org-scoped lookup miss), but four unrelated classes. A route or test doing `except MissionNotFoundError` against the wrong module's import will silently fail to catch it (they're not the same class despite identical names), and any future common handling (e.g. a shared 404 body format) has to be wired into each class separately instead of once against a shared `NotFoundError` in a common module."
  },
  {
    "file": "web/src/screens/LoginScreen.tsx",
    "line": 74,
    "summary": "Hand-rolled danger/error alert `<div>` reproduces ErrorBanner's exact container classes and `role=\"alert\"` instead of rendering `<ErrorBanner message={loginError} />`.",
    "failure_scenario": "ErrorBanner (web/src/components/ErrorBanner.tsx) is imported and used correctly elsewhere in the app, but LoginScreen never imports it and instead pastes `rounded-md border border-danger-border bg-danger-bg px-3 py-2 text-xs text-danger` + role=\"alert\" inline. If ErrorBanner's markup changes (e.g. adding the warning icon it already renders, or an a11y fix to the alert pattern), LoginScreen's login-failure banner won't pick up the change and will visually/accessibility-wise diverge from every other error banner in the app."
  },
  {
    "file": "web/src/screens/MissionCreateScreen.tsx",
    "line": 133,
    "summary": "Same file imports and correctly uses `<ErrorBanner>` at line 139 for the mutation error, but hand-rolls the identical danger-alert markup inline at line 133 for the client-side date-order validation message instead of reusing the component it already has in scope.",
    "failure_scenario": "Because the component is already imported in this exact file, this is a same-file inconsistency, not just cross-file drift: a future change to ErrorBanner's styling/icon/`role` handling will update the mutation-error banner at line 139 but leave the date-order-invalid banner at line 133 with the old look, making the same form show two visually different error styles."
  }
]

